---

Executive Summary

Ohira is an open, AI-first Developer Intelligence Platform that continuously analyzes software projects and transforms source code, infrastructure, documentation, and development workflows into a unified knowledge model.

Unlike traditional documentation tools, Ohira acts as a living intelligence layer that enables developers, engineering teams, and AI assistants to understand software systems quickly and accurately.

The platform combines static analysis, project metadata, plugins, and AI-ready outputs into one extensible ecosystem.


---

Problem Statement

Modern software development suffers from fragmented knowledge:

Documentation becomes outdated.

New developers require weeks to onboard.

AI assistants repeatedly analyze the same repositories.

Engineering decisions are scattered across code, Git history, issue trackers, and conversations.

Project health is difficult to measure consistently.


Organizations lose valuable knowledge whenever developers leave or projects evolve without synchronized documentation.

Ohira addresses these challenges by continuously maintaining an up-to-date understanding of software projects.


---

Vision

To become the universal intelligence layer for software projects, enabling humans and AI systems to collaborate with complete project context.


---

Mission

To make every software project understandable through structured knowledge rather than scattered information.


---

Product Goals

Primary Goals

Analyze software projects automatically.

Build a unified project knowledge model.

Expose structured project intelligence through APIs and CLI tools.

Enable seamless AI integration.

Reduce developer onboarding time.

Automate project reporting.



---

Non-Goals (Version 1)

The initial release will not include:

AI code generation

Cloud deployment services

Source code hosting

CI/CD orchestration

Code editing

Package management

Project management features (Kanban, issues, etc.)


These may be considered in future releases.


